<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Limburg Succession</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1283">1283</a>–<a href="/years/1289">1289</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the Limburg Succession was fought from 1283 to 1289 over the Duchy of Limburg after the death of Duchess Ermengard in 1283. Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-i-duke-of-brabant">John I of Brabant</a>, who had bought the claim of her kinsman Adolf of Berg, faced Count <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reginald-i-count-of-guelders">Reinald I of Guelders</a>, Ermengard's widower, backed by Archbishop <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siegfried-of-westerburg">Siegfried of Westerburg</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> and the count of Luxembourg. John's victory at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-worringen">Battle of Worringen</a> in 1288 won Limburg for Brabant.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-limburg-succession.jpg" alt="War of the Limburg Succession" width="320" height="184" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Worringen_1288.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
